#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0536 expect=noViolation domain=DS
# Rule:Description: Trigger error when there is more than one record per subject per DSSCAT per DSCAT per EPOCH
#note "two DISPOSITION EVENT records with same DSSCAT but distinct EPOCH, so EPOCH is unique per USUBJID/DSSCAT/DSCAT (Positive control added by PLAN-absent-guard-test-hardening P3: CDISC-CG0536 previously had ONLY an expect=skipped fixture, which asserts non-execution and so proved nothing about the rule ever running. Modelled on the retired CORE-family twin's suite.)"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS label=Disposition
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event" format=$DSCAT.
col DSSCAT type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH type=Char label="Epoch"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION | TREATMENT
---
